      "content": "You're right that from a purely logical standpoint, existence and non-existence can look mathematically equivalent—a zero-sum equation. But the flaw is that you're measuring value with a ruler that doesn't exist. In a universe without inherent meaning, *you* get to be the one who assigns the numbers. The choice isn't neutral; it's the first and only act of creation you have. So if you're going to stay, even out of stubbornness, why not make the equation favor you?",
